WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:04.280
IBM's acquisition of a robotic process automation provider,

00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:07.020
the release of IBM Cloud Databases for EnterpriseDB,

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:09.640
and the 2020 Top Rated Awards from TrustRadius

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:11.980
- all on this episode of  IBM Cloud Now.

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:13.460
Hey everyone, I'm Ian,

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:16.200
and I'm excited to bring you the latest and greatest news and announcements

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:17.980
from IBM Cloud.

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:20.600
Recently, IBM announced a definitive agreement

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:24.280
to acquire a Brazilian software provider of robotic process automation,

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:26.820
informally referred to as WDG Automation.

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:30.380
The blog linked below has the full company name in Portuguese.

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:34.200
With this acquisition, we plan to bring WDG Automation’s RPA

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.140
and AI-driven chatbot capabilities

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:39.500
to 2 areas where enterprises have critical automation needs:

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:41.120
transforming business processes

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:43.380
and managing IT operations.

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:46.960
The acquisition will strengthen our AI-infused automation platform

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:49.260
- making it one of the most fully-equipped platforms

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:51.620
for CIOs and COOs looking to

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:53.580
quickly transform and standardize

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:55.100
business and IT operations

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:58.240
for growth, efficiency and resiliency.

00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:01.500
Ultimately, the plan is to include RPA capabilities

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:03.640
across the IBM Cloud Pak® family,

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:06.600
starting with the Cloud Pak® for Automation for business processes

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:10.200
and the Cloud Pak® for Multicloud  Management for IT operations.

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:12.420
For more information about this exciting announcement,

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:14.800
please read the blog linked in the description below.

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:16.960
We'll also be holding an "Ask Me Anything" webinar

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:20.420
with Mike Gilfix, VP of Offering Management for Cloud Integration,

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:24.140
on July 15th, so make sure you register.

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:28.360
Next up, we've got the the release of IBM Cloud Databases for EnterpriseDB.

00:01:28.369 --> 00:01:31.060
EDB PostgreSQL Advanced Server

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:33.580
joins a broad suite of powerful database technologies

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:35.700
on the IBM Cloud Databases platform.

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:38.860
It's a fully managed, production-ready, Database-as-a-Service

00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:43.000
built from the ground up for scale and security of enterprise workloads.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:45.760
Modernizing your data with Databases for EnterpriseDB

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:48.120
enables you to save costs, gain efficiencies,

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:50.540
and power innovation for new applications.

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:52.920
This new release provides compatibility with Oracle,

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:56.000
offers a boost to productivity, and increases security.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:58.820
Hit the link in the description for a full rundown of all the features

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:02.280
and info on how to get rolling with Databases for EnterpriseDB.

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:06.240
And finally, I wanted to close out this episode with a little bit of celebratory news

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:08.900
from the Trust Radius 2020 Top Rated Awards,

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:12.720
where IBM Cloud has been recognized as a leader in several categories.

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:15.800
The Trust Radius Top Rated Awards are the industry standard

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:19.100
for unbiased recognition of B2B technology products,

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:21.920
and are based entirely upon customer feedback.

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:24.140
Since our customers are our top priority

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:26.380
and these awards are based on their unfiltered feedback,

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:29.540
we are thrilled that IBM Cloud Bare Metal Servers,

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:31.040
IBM Cloud Object Storage,

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:34.440
and IBM Cloud Virtual Servers won in the IaaS category.

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:36.940
Additionally, the IBM Cloud Kubernetes Service

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:38.780
won in the Container Management category,

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:41.900
and IBM Cloud Databases won in both the Database-as-a-Service

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:44.220
and Relational Databases categories.

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:47.740
A sincere thanks to each and every one of our customers who submitted reviews,

00:02:47.740 --> 00:02:50.020
because your feedback shapes what we do.

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:52.580
If you'd like to learn more about TrustRadius or the awards,

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:54.800
including the criteria and IBM's scores,

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:56.600
see the link below.

00:02:56.600 --> 00:02:59.500
Thanks for joining me today for this episode of IBM Cloud Now.

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:01.960
If you're interested in learning more about the topics I've covered,

00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:04.740
make sure you explore the links in the description of this video.

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:07.300
And, of course, please don't forget to subscribe to our channel

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:10.260
to stay up-to-date on what's going on in the cloud, now.

